 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "Cohort of six children with Evans syndrome in which one identifiable patient (Table 1 patient 3, 'TNFAIP3 VUS') carries 'a heterozygous missense variant in the TNFAIP3 gene (c.1733C>T; p.Ser578Phe)'.",
 "method_note": "Hand extraction, no script transcription of tables. Table 1 has a 'Patient' column of bare numbers 1-6, so the TNFAIP3 carrier is labelled 'Table 1 #3'; the text's 'one child' with c.1733C>T is linked to Table 1 patient 3 because that is the only row with 'TNFAIP3 VUS' and Table 2 gives exactly 1 TNFAIP3 VUS (linkage is by uniqueness, not stated by name). The other five cohort members have no TNFAIP3 variant and get no rows (cohort_size_as_stated = 6). Mother (carrier, asymptomatic) and father (tested, variant absent) are in-scope relatives. Age at first cytopenia '3' in Table 1 has no unit in the column header; years taken from Table 2/abstract ('Median age at first cytopenia, years'); it is recorded as onset of ITP only, not as the person's age at symptom onset, because one unnamed patient had an IM before first cytopenia. AIHA is not recorded for patient 3: it follows only from the study's ES definition/inclusion criteria, which are not evidence. Sacroiliitis mapped to checklist 'arthritis or arthralgia' (observed); ITP mapped to 'cytopenia (autoimmune)'. 'IM > 1: No' was not used to exclude other checklist items. The mother's 'no history of autoimmune or autoinflammatory disease' is a broad statement and excludes no specific checklist item. Functional evidence: paper states 'Functional validation was not available, and cytokine profiling was not performed', so no assay result (not reported). For the mother's variant row, zygosity/type/pathogenicity are left not reported (stated for the child's variant). Infections (5/6) and DAT findings are unnamed counts and assign nothing to patient 3. No contradictions found.",
